- insert_word_in_sentence treats whitespace tokens as invisible for client-provided word indices: word_idx counts only non-whitespace tokens (words and delimiters). That preserves expected indexing while maintaining exact spacing when interleaving writes.
- Metadata functions that read file bytes (get_file_stats) remain unchanged and will compute word/char counts as before.

